{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0046"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c004): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c004.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0046"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge geography/countries","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/geography__countries.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",790],["+","The second-smallest of the fifteen, the Republic of Moldova, has only two neighbours: Ukraine, which wraps around it on three sides, and Romania to the west, across the Prut. Most Moldovans speak Romanian, and the country declared its independence on 27 August 1991. It too has no sea coast, although a few hundred metres of Danube bank give it a river port at Giurgiulești.\n\n"],["=",217]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",724],["+","Die zweitkleinste der fünfzehn, die Republik Moldau, hat nur zwei Nachbarn: die Ukraine, die sie auf drei Seiten umschließt, und Rumänien im Westen, jenseits des Pruth. Die meisten Moldauer sprechen Rumänisch, und am 27. August 1991 erklärte das Land seine Unabhängigkeit. Auch es hat keine Meeresküste, doch ein paar hundert Meter Donauufer verschaffen ihm bei Giurgiulești einen Flusshafen.\n\n"],["=",211]]}]},
